        "content": "<p>alexcrichton closed <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/issues/14831\">issue #14831</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>For an exported function taking an anonymous map, e.g. <code>f: func(m: map&lt;string, list&lt;string&gt;&gt;)</code>, <code>bindgen!</code> generates:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Rust\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"k\">pub</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">fn</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nf\">call_f</span><span class=\"o\">&lt;</span><span class=\"n\">S</span><span class=\"p\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nc\">AsContextMut</span><span class=\"o\">&gt;</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"o\">&amp;</span><span class=\"bp\">self</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">store</span><span class=\"p\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nc\">S</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">arg0</span><span class=\"p\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nc\">HashMap</span><span class=\"o\">&lt;&amp;</span><span class=\"kt\">str</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">&amp;</span><span class=\"p\">[</span><span class=\"nb\">String</span><span class=\"p\">]</span><span class=\"o\">&gt;</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">-&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">..</span><span class=\"p\">.</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>while for a named <code>type named = map&lt;string, string&gt;</code> it generates <code>call_g(.., arg0: &amp;Named)</code>.</p>\n<p>The anonymous form means a caller holding a <code>HashMap&lt;String, Vec&lt;String&gt;&gt;</code> has to build (and hash) a second map of references just to make the call, and it's inconsistent with both named maps and lists (which are <code>&amp;[T]</code>). Generating <code>&amp;HashMap&lt;K, V&gt;</code> with owned keys and values, the way lists are handled, would fix both. Since this changes generated signatures it seems worth settling before <code>map</code> is enabled by default.<br>\n</p>\n</blockquote>",
